{
 "_doc": "Bannerline art data (stream C, PLAN \u00a714/\u00a716). How each unit's `model` ref in units.json becomes a 3D body. `chibi2` refs: start from a Chibi 2 preset (`bases`, avatar-3d/data/chibi2-presets.json by name) or a Farhold warband member (`warband` = a def id in prototypes/farhold/data/warbands.json, read-only), dress it as a class (`outfit`, avatar-3d/data/class-outfits.json), then apply `units.<id>.parts` slot overrides and the race `paint` (top/cape/hat colour swaps). `creature` refs: the race's `creatures` table names a designed look in avatar-3d/data/creature-variants.json (falling back to the bare type). `scale` is a suggested world scale so a T4 reads bigger than a T1 from the RTS camera; the view may ignore it. `heroes` are the four hero bodies. Read by js/view/unit-looks.js only; the sim never reads this file. `heroes.<id>.team` names the slots painted in the player's colour (`{slot: 'color'|'color2'}`) by `forHero(id, { color })` \u2014 heroes are the one exception to never-recolour, because the owner wants a hero to read as his at a glance (5 heroes x 6 slot colours at most 30 Chibi 2 templates). `forms.<hero>.<form id>` is the creature look (creature-variants.json) a hero turns into while shaped (heroes.json skills `form.id`). `pets.<pet id>` is the creature look for a hero's summon (heroes.json `pets`).",
